 "notes": "Hold-out (H2-D20), read before the extractor ran. Scope: the recipe and organizer routers (mealie/routes/recipe/, mealie/routes/organizers/), 69 routes. mealie/routes/__init__.py builds router = APIRouter(prefix=\"/api\") and includes each package's router; recipe/__init__.py includes exports and recipe_crud_routes as they are (each has prefix=\"/recipes\") and comments, bulk_actions, shared_routes and timeline_events under prefix=\"/recipes\"; organizers/__init__.py is APIRouter(prefix=\"/organizers\") over categories, tags and tools. Routers are the project's own APIRouter subclasses (UserAPIRouter, MealieCrudRoute as route_class) and most routes are methods of class-based views (@controller(router) class X: @router.get(..)), some decorators over several lines. Moved to the corpus by F1.14 (2026-10-18), which reads the project's router classes: a class whose bases reach APIRouter (UserAPIRouter, AdminAPIRouter, in mealie/routes/_base/routers.py) builds a router, its prefix read by what its __init__ hands super().__init__ (prefix=prefix: the call's argument). The checked sample was refreshed: the 7 items take their router's prefix at the same evidence line — 3 in the expected list, 4 outside its scope judged from the code (/api/admin/groups/{group_id}/ai-providers/providers/{provider_id}, /api/groups/migrations, /api/households/mealplans/rules/{item_id}, /api/users/password).",
